<h1>Why Choose This Online Training?</h1>

<h2>A grounded teaching foundation</h2>

<p>Seb is the lead and sole instructor of the 200-Hour Online Qigong Teacher Training. He has been practising Qigong since 2010 and teaching since 2018, with many students trained to date and senior tutor experience at the Traditional Thai Massage Association Japan and the Shivaga Traditional Medical School in Japan.</p>

<p>His Qigong training has taken him to masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland, with named lineage teachers including Ma Zheng in China, Alex Cox and Soichiro Watanabe in Tokyo, and Des Lawton in Scotland, as well as a few quiet, unnamed masters along the way. He has gone on to lead Qigong groups in Tokyo, Fukuoka, Vienna, Seoul and Da Nang.</p>

<p>His teaching is precise, unhurried and grounded in the forms themselves. The work he leads sits within a clear Traditional Chinese Medicine framework - meridians, acupoints, the Five Elements, the cultivation of Jing, Qi and Shen - taught in a way that gives the body something to do and the mind something to verify. Where the popular versions of Qigong have grown vague, his teaching stays specific.</p>

<p>Seb is also a Therapeutic Thai Bodywork instructor accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018, and has trained extensively in TCM Reflexology. Both inform a hands-on understanding of how the body's energy lines respond to careful, structured work. His path began with Yoga in 1997, and the combination of long-form Yoga practice, classical Qigong and Therapeutic Thai Bodywork gives his teaching an unusual depth across both Indian and Chinese traditions of working with the body and its energies.</p>

